# Static routing for the release-digest endpoint — copied to the
# assets root by scripts/build_worker_site.py (Workers assets honor
# _redirects ONLY at the root, exactly like _headers). The docs are
# .json files under api/digests/** (the tracked
# packages/pairing-relay/digests/ tree); the client paths are
# extensionless BY DESIGN (a real file at /api/digests/<channel> would
# collide with the channel's own directory — see relay-core's digests
# module), so the pointers are redirected onto the .json files.
#
# With /api/digests* NEGATED out of run_worker_first (wrangler.toml;
# negative patterns take precedence) these two rules make a served
# channel's lookups pure static asset traffic: the 302 plus the .json
# file, ZERO worker invocations — no read budget, rate limiter or KV
# quota anywhere on the path. Deployed app clients follow redirects
# transparently (reqwest's default policy). A miss — unpublished
# channel or unknown tag — redirects onto a missing .json, the assets
# layer misses, and the request falls through to the worker's digests
# handler, which answers the same gated, edge-cached 404 the direct
# route always did (crates/relay-worker/src/digests.rs).
#
# A tag containing dots (v0.6.5) still matches :tag — a path
# placeholder stops at `/` only.
/api/digests/:channel /api/digests/:channel/latest.json 302
/api/digests/:channel/:tag /api/digests/:channel/:tag.json 302
